# Titan Pocket: let TrustKernel prepare its secure storage, added by 65-extra-init.
#
# The vendor's trustkernel.rc makes /data/vendor/t6 (and fs/, app/) only from
# the ro.crypto.state triggers for "unencrypted" and "encrypted". Under Halium
# vold reports "unsupported", so none fires, the directories never exist, and
# teed has nowhere to keep a TA's storage. The first TA that asks for it waits
# for good: on 11 Nov 2026 the fingerprint HAL
# (android.hardware.biometrics.fingerprint@2.1-service, Sunwave sensor on the
# TrustKernel TEE) sat in uninterruptible sleep in tee_supp_cmd() from its
# first second, never registered IBiometricsFingerprint, and the fingerprint
# reader did nothing. With this it registers at once and biomd finds it.
#
# Mode 1 is the one trustkernel.rc itself sets for an unencrypted /data.
on property:ro.crypto.state=unsupported
    setprop vendor.trustkernel.fs.mode 1
    setprop vendor.trustkernel.fs.state prepare
